<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="energy_maritime_chokepoi::crude_export_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger perceived unity among allied states enables coordinated economic measures and joint interdiction/logistics (e.g., sanctions enforcement, naval escorts/interdictions) that constrain a belligerent's ability to export crude.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="iran_proxy_escalation::foreign_military_presenc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A visible weakening of coalition unity over the Ukraine war (policy splits, delayed commitments) leads partner states to reduce or pause regional rotations and burden-sharing, producing a measurable drop in foreign force posture in the Middle East theater.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="north_korea_missiles::external_influence_index" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger and more visible cohesion among US/ROK/Japan deterrent postures reduces opportunities for Moscow and Beijing to expand political and operational leverage over Pyongyang, lowering external patron influence on DPRK decision-making.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">north_korea_missiles</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="us_china_tech_trade::compute_concentration" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter security alignment among the US and partners drives coordinated procurement, certification and network‑trusting arrangements that favor a small set of vetted Western cloud and HPC providers, increasing market concentration of high‑end compute.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
