<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="energy_maritime_chokepoi::shipping_freight_rates" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating kinetic and non-kinetic hostilities raise perceived operational and insurance risk and force longer routings or escorts, which increases charter costs and insurance premiums embedded in freight rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">energy_maritime_chokepoi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="north_korea_missiles::arms_flow_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">As Iranian-proxy fighting intensifies, Iran and its proxies accelerate urgent procurement of rockets and missile components, prompting increased clandestine arms transfers from alternative suppliers including North Korea and raising the overall volume of weapons flows tied to the crisis.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">north_korea_missiles</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalation by Iran-linked proxies correlates with accelerated transfers of drones, precision munitions and technical assistance from Iran (and its networks) to Russia, enabling an increase in the tempo and destructiveness of kinetic strikes in Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::conflict_intensity" target="us_china_tech_trade::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising kinetic and asymmetric hostilities raise geopolitical and operational risk perceptions among investors and institutional LPs, causing a pullback or reallocation of financing away from cross-border and high-risk AI ventures linked to the affected region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
