  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sharp rise in maritime attacks forces Western governments to reallocate naval assets, munitions stocks and political bandwidth to secure merchant shipping and partners in the Middle East, producing measurable delays and down‑prioritisation of weapons deliveries and financing destined for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
